      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Coordinate removal of damaged surface, subgrade prep, and base course placement",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 367549,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Phase 1 update: We've started T3, removing the damaged road surface. Let's keep the Progress and Quantities Tracking Sheet A3 updated hourly. What's a realistic target for cubic meters removed per shift?",
            "mentions": [
              6789,
              70034,
              192754
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3",
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 70034,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Based on the excavator size and truck cycle times, I think we can aim for 150 cubic meters per 8-hour shift. That should keep us on track.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 384719,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "150 sounds right. We can probably push for 170 if we get a good run.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 367549,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "Let's stick with 150 as the official target to keep it achievable and safe. Decision: We will target 150 cubic meters per shift for surface removal and subgrade prep, logged in A3.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 192754,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Team, we have a problem. The subgrade in the northern section is very soft. The excavator is sinking a bit.",
            "mentions": [
              367549,
              6789
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "warning",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 367549,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "Thanks for the flag. How large is the area? Can you take a photo?",
            "mentions": [
              192754
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 384719,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "We should just dig it out and fill it with more base course material. That's the fastest way.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 6789,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "That might not be enough if it's a deeper issue. We should not proceed with T4 in that area. We need to properly assess the weak zone. I recommend we excavate a test pit, about 1 meter deep, to see the soil profile. Depending on what we find, we might need to use a geotextile layer before placing new base material. This will prevent future failure.",
            "mentions": [
              367549
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 192754,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "It is about 10 meters long. I will get a photo.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 367549,
            "reply_to": "M26",
            "text": "That's the right approach. Let's not rush this and have to redo it later. Decision: For any weak subgrade zones, we will excavate a test pit to assess the soil and use a geotextile layer if required before backfilling. Pausing T4 in that specific section for now.",
            "mentions": [
              6789,
              192754
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 168084,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "I have done the safety checklist A2 for the day.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 70034,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "Understood. We'll continue with T3 in the other sections while that assessment is happening.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 6789,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "I'll oversee the test pit excavation and report back with findings and a recommendation within the hour.",
