      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Plan and monitor drainage upgrades and pipe bedding works",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 70034,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, we've started on T5, cleaning out the existing drainage channels. In the eastern section, the channel is partially collapsed. The standard detail in A5 might not work here. How should we proceed?",
            "mentions": [
              367549,
              6789
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5",
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 168084,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "what does A5 say to do for this?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 384719,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Can we just patch it with concrete?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 6789,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "A patch won't provide the structural integrity we need. A5 shows two details: Detail A for new channels and Detail B for repairs. Since this is a collapse, we should treat it as a new installation. I recommend we excavate the collapsed section completely and rebuild it using Detail A from the sketches in A5, ensuring proper pipe bedding and compaction around the new pipe.",
            "mentions": [
              367549
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 367549,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "I agree. Let's go with the more robust solution to avoid future issues. Decision: We will use Detail A from A5 (new installation) for any sections where existing drainage channels are damaged or collapsed.",
            "mentions": [
              6789,
              70034
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 70034,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "Okay, understood. We'll start excavating that section. Before we backfill, when do you want to inspect it?",
            "mentions": [
              367549
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 192754,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "I can help with the digging.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 367549,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Good question. We need to do interim quality checks as part of T10. Let's set up two mandatory inspection points for all new drainage works.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 6789,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "I suggest two hold points: first, after the pipe is laid on its bedding to check slope and alignment. Second, after the initial surround is placed and compacted, but before the final backfill. We can use the Interim Quality Inspection Checklist A6 for this.",
            "mentions": [
              367549
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 367549,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "Perfect. That's our process then. Decision: We will have two formal inspection points for drainage before backfilling: 1) after pipe laying, and 2) after placing the surround. These will be recorded in A6.",
            "mentions": [
              6789,
              70034
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 168084,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "ok i will get the checklist ready.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 70034,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Got it. I'll call for the first inspection once the pipe is in place this afternoon.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          }
        ],
