      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Manage asphalt paving, compaction, and quality checks under time pressure",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 367549,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Heads up team. First asphalt delivery is scheduled for tomorrow morning to start T6. The weather forecast is showing a 40% chance of rain. We need to be prepared.",
            "mentions": [
              6789,
              70034,
              168084,
              384719
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "cloud_with_rain",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 384719,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "We can't afford to lose a day. We should just pave unless it's pouring down.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 70034,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "I'm not so sure. If the base is wet, we'll have serious problems with compaction. The roller won't be effective and we could get steam voids in the asphalt. It's a big risk.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 168084,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "what is the rule for rain? is there a procedure?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 6789,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "He's right. We need clear go/no-go criteria. I propose the following: No paving if there is standing water on the base course. Paving can proceed in light drizzle only if the asphalt mix temperature at the paver is maintained above 135 degrees Celsius. If heavy rain starts, all paving must stop immediately. This protects the quality of the final surface.",
            "mentions": [
              367549
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 367549,
            "reply_to": "M50",
            "text": "That's a clear, technical, and safe rule. Let's make that official. Decision: Paving is a 'no-go' if there's standing water or heavy rain. Paving can proceed in light drizzle only if asphalt temp is >135C at the paver.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 70034,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "Understood. I'll make sure the temperature gun is ready. We also need to coordinate the equipment well, as per T8, so the roller is ready as soon as the paver lays the mat.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 367549,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "Exactly. And once a section is paved, we need to get it open to essential traffic quickly. What are the absolute minimum checks we need to complete before we can do that?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M54",
            "speaker_id": 192754,
            "reply_to": "M53",
            "text": "We need to check it is smooth.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M55",
            "speaker_id": 6789,
            "reply_to": "M54",
